V15 Copilot semantic + cross-city authority: TESTS ONLY.

Every file below is new (new file mode / --- /dev/null), so this patch
adds only test-support modules and test modules. It changes no product
code, no schema, no route and no configuration, and it deletes nothing.
There is therefore nothing for it to conflict with in the Codex worktree.

Guarantees it encodes:
  * hypothetical (WHAT_IF) and preference messages never create a real Event;
  * only DISRUPTION_REPORT may create one, and only from a present-tense report;
  * authority-override attempts never receive a mutation-permitting policy;
  * commitment-touching requests always require confirmation;
  * no copilot path moves PlanVersion / Commitment / Booking / payment state;
  * cross-city journeys never inherit another city's locale, place hints or money unit;
  * the two named minimal pairs never collapse into one route.

Known V14 gaps are recorded as named xfail(strict=False) markers rather than
failures, so this patch is green on today's tree and turns green-to-XPASS as
the gaps are fixed.

Apply:  git apply patches/V15_COPILOT_TESTS_ONLY.patch
Verify: git apply --check patches/V15_COPILOT_TESTS_ONLY.patch

